Have you ever worked with Daemons in Linux?

Yes, you have worked with Daemons when you started learning Linux

Daemon is a background process that runs without direct user interaction. Think of it like a helper doing its job in the background. 

I worked with Daemons while setting up Nginx on a Linux Server. When you start Nginx, it launches as a Daemon. This means it is running in the background and keeps serving web requests even after you log out of the terminal.

It is a key part of how Linux works efficiently.
